   <section class='publication-abstract'><h2 class='publication-abstract-heading'>Abstract</h2><div class='publication-abstract-body'><span class='pplb7t-x-x-109'>Task-agnostic pretraining </span>trains a model on synthetic or procedural tasks
selected for reusable structure rather than for one downstream objective. It seeks
patterns that transfer across later tasks, including compositional rules, state
transitions, symbolic operations, and compression strategies. Prepretraining is
one implementation: the task-agnostic phase runs before training on natural
data.</div></section>
